WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.804
Moderate impact is central to many FedRAMP conversations because many federal cloud services process information or support use cases with meaningful sensitivity or mission importance.

2
00:00:11.804 --> 00:00:24.125
Moderate does not mean extreme, but it does mean the service needs stronger governance, implementation discipline, testing, documentation, and ongoing monitoring than a lower-impact scenario.

3
00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:30.322
It is often the practical middle ground for federal SaaS, platform, and infrastructure offerings.

4
00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:48.103
A Moderate baseline expectation touches many operational themes: identity and access control, audit logging, configuration management, vulnerability handling, encryption, incident response, contingency planning, risk assessment, vendor operations, and change management.

5
00:00:48.103 --> 00:00:52.529
The details depend on the architecture, but the pattern is consistent.

6
00:00:52.529 --> 00:00:59.981
The provider must be able to show not only that policies exist, but that the system operates according to those policies.

7
00:00:59.981 --> 00:01:03.817
Moderate work affects engineering and operations directly.

8
00:01:03.817 --> 00:01:16.138
Engineers may need to design clearer boundaries, strengthen tenant separation, centralize logging, reduce manual configuration, document inherited controls, and create repeatable evidence.

9
00:01:16.138 --> 00:01:23.442
Security teams need vulnerability workflows, monitoring routines, incident response records, and risk tracking.

10
00:01:23.442 --> 00:01:30.894
Product teams need to understand what commitments are being made to agencies and what future features may change scope.

11
00:01:30.894 --> 00:01:34.140
A common mistake is treating Moderate as paperwork.

12
00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.271
The package matters, but the package should reflect a real system.

13
00:01:38.271 --> 00:01:49.928
If the service cannot produce evidence, cannot explain responsibilities, cannot track vulnerabilities, or cannot monitor meaningful changes, the documentation will not hold up well.

14
00:01:49.928 --> 00:01:59.445
The baseline should become an operating model: protect the service, document honestly, assess the controls, and keep monitoring after authorization.
